<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zheng He</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zheng He was a Chinese admiral and court <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuch</a> who led seven great maritime expeditions for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a> between 1405 and 1433. His fleets of large treasure ships sailed through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> as far as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>, establishing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tributary-system">tributary relations</a> and projecting imperial prestige. Accounts of the Ming Empire treat the voyages as a high point of Ming maritime power, though they were later discontinued.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zheng-he.jpg" alt="Zheng He" width="280" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marcin Konsek · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2016_Malakka,_Stadhuys_(09).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
